{
  "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
  "total_duration_s": 82.9,
  "total_frames_30fps": 2487,
  "segments": [
    {
      "seg_id": "N01",
      "text": "NASA's Kepler space telescope revealed over three hundred million rocky habitable worlds across our galaxy. Billions of older stars formed long before our Sun ignited.",
      "rate": "+3%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 0.1,
      "end": 9.512,
      "duration": 9.412,
      "pause_after": 0.24,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N02",
      "text": "Even crawling at one percent of light speed, a starship fleet crosses the galaxy in ten million years. In cosmic time, that's a blink\u2014so physicist Enrico Fermi asked: where is everybody?",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 9.752,
      "end": 21.508,
      "duration": 11.756,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N03",
      "text": "Since nineteen sixty, giant radio dishes and optical telescopes have scanned thousands of nearby star systems. Across more than sixty years of listening, confirmed alien signals equal zero.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 21.768,
      "end": 33.124,
      "duration": 11.355,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N04",
      "text": "To explain why alien life feels so rare, Robin Hanson proposed the Great Filter. Between dead rock and starflight sits at least one brutal barrier almost nothing survives.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+1Hz",
      "start": 33.384,
      "end": 43.76,
      "duration": 10.376,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N05",
      "text": "If that filter lies behind us, we already hit the cosmic jackpot. On early Earth, simple microbes stalled for nearly two billion years before two cells merged into complex life.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 44.02,
      "end": 54.773,
      "duration": 10.754,
      "pause_after": 0.28,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N06",
      "text": "The darker option puts the Great Filter ahead of us. Perhaps rocky worlds sprout intelligent species often\u2014only to wipe themselves out once nuclear or climate tech arrives.",
      "rate": "+2%",
      "pitch": "+1Hz",
      "start": 55.053,
      "end": 65.152,
      "duration": 10.098,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N07",
      "text": "Still, radio silence doesn't prove we're alone: astronomers calculate our searches have sampled barely a glass from the cosmic ocean.",
      "rate": "-2%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
      "start": 65.412,
      "end": 72.73,
      "duration": 7.318,
      "pause_after": 0.28,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N08",
      "text": "Until one signal breaks the quiet, Earth remains the only voice we know. Tonight, our telescopes keep listening across three hundred million silent worlds.",
      "rate": "-1%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
      "start": 73.01,
      "end": 82.67,
      "duration": 9.66,
      "pause_after": 0.24,
      "emphasis_words": []
    }
  ],
